A window launched by a trampoline (a source activity that has not drawn a frame yet, e.g. Files' LauncherActivity, which starts FilesActivity in a new task and finishes) takes the trampoline task's place instead of cascading 75 dp from it, and tasks whose top activity has not drawn yet are left out of the conflict check (otherwise the window that took the trampoline's place is pushed 1/16 of the screen away from the still-alive trampoline task). On Microsoft's WSA Files opens one cascade step (+94 px) from the previous window; without this patch it was two (+188 px, the second step from AOSP's own source-activity branch) — and with only the first hunk +254,+194 px (the conflict check). Verified live on aosp17-gsi through the path A counterpart (WsaCascade): +94,+94 px. On top of 0026+0027. Generated with diff -u from the lineage-21 tree (android-14 based); the same hunks apply to android-13..16 and LineageOS 20–22 (only line numbers differ). Android 16 QPR2 (LineageOS 23.2), Android 17 and LineageOS 24 — 0028-trampoline-takes-source-place-a17.diff: there the conflict check walks leaf tasks with isVisibleRequested(), and this diff's second hunk still applies with fuzz but lands in the wrong method (adjustBoundsToAvoidConflict, no `task` there) — the build fails with "cannot find symbol: variable task".

